# 1. Initialize Git repository
git init

# 2. Configure Git
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your-email@gmail.com"

# 3. Create a file
Set-Content index.html "Welcome to the Main Branch"

# 4. Stage and commit initial file
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"

# 5. Create feature branch
git branch feature

# 6. Switch to feature branch
git checkout feature

# 7. Modify the same file in feature branch
Set-Content index.html "Welcome to the Feature Branch"

# 8. Stage and commit feature changes
git add .
git commit -m "Updated file in feature branch"

# 9. Switch back to main branch
git checkout main

# 10. Modify the same file differently
Set-Content index.html "Welcome to the Main Project"

# 11. Stage and commit main branch changes
git add .
git commit -m "Updated file in main branch"

# 12. Merge feature branch
git merge feature

At Step 12, Git should display a merge conflict.
Resolve the conflict
Open index.html in VS Code. You will see conflict markers similar to:
<<<<<<< HEAD
Welcome to the Main Project
=======
Welcome to the Feature Branch
>>>>>>> feature

Manually replace the entire content with
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to the Library Management Project</h1>
</body>
</html>

# 13. Check resolved file status
git status

# 14. Stage resolved file
git add index.html

# 15. Complete merge
git commit -m "Resolved merge conflict"

# 16. Verify merge result
git status

# 17. View final commit history
git log --oneline --graph --all

# 18. View merge commit details
git show
